		;
	skos:definition """In Mechanical Design, physical product structure, product geometry, as well as all specifications are defined.
This includes shape, dimensioning and tolerancing, material (including semi-finished parts and treatment), surface and edge specifications.
Mechanical design is usually conducted using a mechanical CAD system."""@en ;
	.

<http://www.omg.org/spec/CASCaRA/activities/ProductDevelopment/ProductDesign/SoftwareEngineering>
