cas-act:VerificationValidationUsingSimulation
	a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:subClassOf cas:Entity ;
	rdfs:label
		"Verification & Validation using Simulation"@en ,
		"Verifikation & Validierung durch Simulation"@de
		;
	dcterms:modified "2023-03-10T07:09:37Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
	skos:definition """Modeling and simulation (M&S) is the domain-specific use of models (e.g., physical, mathematical, or logical representation of a system, entity, phenomenon, or process) as a basis for simulations to develop data utilized for management or technical decision making.
Simulation may include finite elements analysis, fluid analysis, DMU simulation, kinematics simulation, as well as simulation based on software prototypes. It also includes X-in-the-Loop (XiL), using integrated design and simulation models and capabilities.
Verification aims at the demonstration of product compliance to the specified design requirements.
Validation aims at the demonstration of conformance to stakeholder requirements.
Description based on: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modeling_and_simulation, ISO 29148, ISO 15288"""@en ;
	.

cas-act:VerificationValidationUsingTest
	a owl:Class ;
	rdfs:subClassOf cas:Entity ;
	rdfs:label
		"Verification & Validation using Test"@en ,
		"Verifikation & Validierung durch Test"@de
		;
	dcterms:modified "2023-03-10T07:29:10Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
	skos:definition """While simulation is based on virtual models, testing is based on prototypes and samples.
Verification is to demonstrate product compliance to the specified design requirements. Validation is to demonstrate conformance to stakeholder requirements.
Description based on ISO 29148, resp. ISO 15288"""@en ;
	.

